        "math_academy_id": "q-74128",
        "problem": "Given the vector $u=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$, find $\u2016-2u\u2016.$",
        "worked_solution": "Remember that we can factor a constant out of the norm, provided that we take the absolute value of the constant:\n\n$$\n\u2016ku\u2016=|k|\\cdot \u2016u\u2016\n$$\n\nUsing this fact and the formula for the norm, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2016-2u\u2016 & =|-2|\\cdot \u2016u\u2016 \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{{u}_{1}^{2}+{u}_{2}^{2}+{u}_{3}^{2}+{u}_{4}^{2}+{u}_{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{5}^{2}+{3}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{4+1+25+9+1} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{40} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 2\\sqrt{10} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "actual_result": "Correct",
